---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const steps = [
  { label: 'In Claude Code, install the plugin', code: '/plugin install aos --marketplace aos-engineer/harness' },
  { label: 'In your terminal, install the CLI you approve gates with', code: 'npm install -g aos-harness@next' },
  { label: 'Back in Claude Code, start a run', code: '/aos:run add a --shout flag to the greet command' },
];

const pillars = [
  {
    title: 'Staged runs',
    body: 'A brief becomes a spike (frame, probe) or a bounded change (design, build, verify). Each stage ends at a gate, and the next stage opens only when that gate passes.',
    href: '/docs/concepts/',
  },
  {
    title: 'Observed evidence',
    body: 'Hooks record the test runs the agent actually executes, fingerprinted against the git tree. A claimed result, or one from an older tree, cannot pass a gate that asks for an observed one.',
    href: '/docs/concepts/',
  },
  {
    title: 'Human approvals',
    body: 'Design approval happens with aos approve in your own terminal. The agent can ask for an approval but cannot grant one: aos approve refuses to run without a terminal or inside an agent session.',
    href: '/docs/cli/',
  },
  {
    title: 'Guarded actions',
    body: 'Push and pull request creation wait for the verify gate, deploys never run inside a run, and a spike can never push. Each stage limits where file-edit tools may write.',
    href: '/docs/concepts/',
  },
];
---

<Base title="AOS: staged gates for coding agents" version="1.0">
  <section class="px-6 pt-12 pb-12 md:pt-[96px] md:pb-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[820px] text-center">
      <p class="text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--color-signal)]">AOS 1.0 prerelease</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-[32px] sm:text-[40px] md:text-5xl font-extrabold leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-[var(--color-text)]">
        Staged gates for coding agents, closed only on evidence
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-[18px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] max-w-[680px] mx-auto">
        AOS runs inside Claude Code as a plugin. It splits work into stages and closes each one only on evidence: test runs it observed itself, reviews the agent records, and approvals only you can give.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 justify-center">
        <a href="/docs/getting-started/" class="btn-primary w-full sm:w-auto">Get started</a>
        <a href="/docs/security/" class="btn-secondary w-full sm:w-auto">What it defends, and what it does not</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 pb-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[720px]">
      <ol class="space-y-4">
        {steps.map((step, i) => (
          <li class="bg-[var(--color-surface)] border border-[var(--color-border)] rounded-lg p-4 px-5">
            <p class="text-[13px] font-medium text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">{i + 1}. {step.label}</p>
            <pre class="!bg-transparent !border-0 !p-0 mt-2 text-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>{step.code}</code></pre>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[13px] text-[var(--color-text-muted)] text-center">
        Needs Claude Code 2.1.295 or later, <a class="underline" href="https://bun.sh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Bun</a> 1.3.11 or later on your PATH, and git.
        <a class="underline" href="/docs/getting-started/">Full walkthrough</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-[var(--color-surface)] border-y border-[var(--color-border)] px-6 py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1100px]">
      <h2 class="text-[28px] font-bold text-[var(--color-text)] text-center">How a run works</h2>
      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        {pillars.map((p) => (
          <a href={p.href} class="bg-[var(--color-bg)] border border-[var(--color-border)] rounded-xl p-6 card-hover no-underline block">
            <h3 class="text-[18px] font-bold text-[var(--color-text)]">{p.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-[14px] text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mt-2">{p.body}</p>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[760px]">
      <h2 class="text-[24px] font-bold text-[var(--color-text)]">A guardrail, not a security boundary</h2>
      <p class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mt-3">
        AOS keeps a cooperating agent on the process and makes skipping a step visible. It does not contain a determined one: an agent with shell access can reach the run log through processes the hooks never see, and the shell guards read command text. Every run is an append-only, hash-chained log under <code>.aos/runs/</code>, so an edit that breaks the chain is detected, but the chain is not signed.
        <a class="underline text-[var(--color-signal)]" href="/docs/security/">Read the security model</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="text-[15px] text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mt-4">
        This release supports Claude Code, and spike and bounded runs; briefs the reference pack classifies as architectural are refused.
        The <a class="underline text-[var(--color-signal)]" href="https://github.com/aos-engineer/harness/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">release notes</a> list what is not in it yet.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
